{
  "analysis": "I have all the information needed to write the freestanding libc shim. The undefined symbols are known, and I understand the VM's syscall conventions and file handling. I need to determine the FILE struct's _fileno offset for my fopen/fwrite implementations, then write the comprehensive libc shim and build.",
  "plan": "Check the FILE struct _fileno offset using the cross-compiler. Then create libc_min.c implementing all undefined symbols: syscall wrappers, memory allocator, string functions, printf family, file I/O, stdlib, ctype, errno, math, and helper functions. Compile everything and test on the VM.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /tmp/check_file.c <<'EOF'\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stddef.h>\nvolatile int off = (int)offsetof(FILE, _fileno);\nvolatile int sz = (int)sizeof(FILE);\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc-12 -ffreestanding -static -march=mips1 -mfp32 -I. -c /tmp/check_file.c -o /tmp/check_file.o && mipsel-linux-gnu-nm /tmp/check_file.o | grep -E 'off|sz'\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=1290 && NR<=1340 {print NR \":\" $0}' /app/vm.js\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
